  "response": "The area of a triangle is given by the formula: \n\n$$\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height}$$\n\nIn this case, the base and height are the lengths of the two shorter sides, which are 3 cm and 4 cm. \n\nTherefore, the area is:\n\n$$\\frac{1}{2} \\times 3 \\times 4 = 6 \\text{ cm}^2$$\n\nSo, the area of the triangle is 6 cm\u00b2.",
